Today is Saturday.
I finish my morning shift at the neighbourhood café.
My colleague Sunita says goodbye to me.
I come out of the café onto the street.
The afternoon weather is very sticky today.
There is a lot of humidity in the air.
The afternoon heat is more than the morning.
The Mumbai monsoon is going to arrive soon.
I need some essential clothes for the rain.
I walk to the bus stop.
I board the red bus.
I give twenty rupees to the conductor bhaiya and take a ticket.
The bus takes me to the main market of the city.
There are many clothes shops here.
The city shops are bigger than my neighbourhood's shops.
I need a big raincoat and a cotton shirt.
There is a lot of crowd in the market today.
I quickly go inside a clothes shop.
